       - a soft accent-glow bloom + warmed border + deeper shadow on hover, so
         the card reads as rising. The rise is shadow-based, not transform-based:
         these <li>s carry data-reveal, whose .is-visible sets transform:none on
         the same element and would cancel a transform lift.
       - the featured (Signature) tier carries an always-on accent glow and an
         accent border so the recommended option draws the eye at rest.
     Transitions are disabled by the global reduced-motion rule; every rest
     state is complete and legible without motion. Decorative only (text and
     contrast untouched), and a top-edge rule, never a side stripe. */
  .tier-card {
    transition:
      box-shadow 0.32s ease,
      border-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  /* Top accent rule on the top edge, clipped to the rounded corners by the
     card's own overflow-hidden. Faint and slightly short at rest, drawing to
